It's not too difficult.  Would the players even notice, though?

After all, right now the chance of loading a bones is fixed; it would
only be 'which' bones that would change.

Increasing the frequency by which bones are loaded would allow the
players to notice, but also might cause a significant disruption in 
gameplay; right now bones tend to end the game as they're either a 
huge positive boost (wizard bones) or kill you (wizard bones with 
blinded Demogorgon).  Increasing that frequency doesn't strike me as
being a good thing.

Perhaps there needs to be a change as to exactly what sort of stuff is
left behind in bones, to render them more of an "interesting" event as
opposed to a game-ender?

